  "sourceNotes": [
    "An official NWS Frost Advisory remains active for Boyle County, Kentucky, through 9 AM EDT. No official NWS alert is active for the configured Clemson point; the Fire Danger Statement mentioned by NWS Greenville-Spartanburg is confined to northeast Georgia.",
    "College of DuPage Southeast radar imagery showed no organized precipitation over Central Kentucky or Upstate South Carolina. True-color satellite imagery showed both target regions largely cloud-free, with the main offshore cloud shield east of the Carolinas.",
    "The October 19, 2026 Kentucky Weather Center post “A Gorgeous Week for Fall Colors” was consulted as independent supplemental analysis. It supports a dry blocked pattern, highs mainly from the middle 60s to lower 70s, and another frosty Kentucky start; it is not an official source.",
    "KDVK parsed temperature fields were quality-controlled as null, so its official raw METAR temperature/dewpoint group (02/02 Celsius) was converted to 36°F. KCEU had not reported since October 16, so current Upstate conditions use KLQK and KAND; KCEU remains a verification station when official reporting resumes.",
    "Official point forecasts, observations, office discussions and the GFS/ECMWF point benchmarks agree on a dry 72-hour pattern. The modest model spread in Upstate highs and nighttime lows is represented by the calibrated ranges; no unresolved material source conflict remains.",
    "HRRR, RAP, NAM, NAM 3-km Nest, GFS, GEFS and ECMWF availability was verified from official run files; College of DuPage panels supplied common visual context.",
    "Tempest data was not used for Upstate observations, verification, calibration or adjustment.",
    "Official NWS alerts are separate from this independent analysis. Independent hazard probabilities and fire-spread concerns do not constitute watches, warnings or advisories."
  ],
